I don't know about the conducts, but score is broken.  There have been
several games that ended at precisely 2^31-1, the maximum score possible
before it goes negative (twos-complement signed value, a phenomenon that 
probably seems really strange if you don't understand the computer
science behind it.)

So the challenge is to keep your score below half that value (because
ascending will double it), and the real challenge is setting up your end
game so that in the score file, you have *exactly* 2147483647 points.

I think I'd like to go for a zero point ascension instead.  The
challenge has equal difficulty.  It appears to be "easier" to hit a
specific score by dying than by ascending, since the score calculation
is fairly complicated, and that's risky when you must precisely hit a
certain score.  

I think Zadir's score will stand at #1 for a really long time (on the
nethack.alt.org server), but I hope he gets bumped from #1 by someone
who gets the same score, but ascends.

